1 Overview and Architecture
***************************

'go-flowAPI' compiles as a zero-dependency pure-Go static binary
('CGO_ENABLED=0') embedding the 'go-flow' pipeline execution engine and
relational drivers for Microsoft SQL Server / Azure SQL, PostgreSQL,
MySQL / MariaDB, SQLite, and Oracle.

Packages install isolated under '/opt/flow-api' on Unix platforms and
'C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow API\' on Windows so binaries and
manuals never conflict with system packages or with the 'go-flow' CLI
package ('/opt/flow').

'go-flowAPI' does not auto-create database tables at startup.  Before
starting the service against a new database, apply the schema DDL in
'/opt/flow-api/share/doc/SCHEMA.md' or the ready-to-run SQL scripts in
'/opt/flow-api/share/sql/'.


