2 Invoking 'go-flowAPI'
***********************

Synopsis:

     go-flowAPI [-env-file PATH] [-dsn URI] [-addr HOST:PORT] [options...]
     go-flowAPI -hash-password "PlaintextPassword"

Command-Line Flags:

'-dsn URI'
     Database connection string override ('FLOW_API_DSN').
'-addr ADDR'
     HTTP TCP listen address, default ':8080' ('FLOW_API_ADDR' / 'PORT').
'-env-file PATH'
     Load unset 'KEY=VALUE' environment variables from PATH
     ('FLOW_API_ENV_FILE').
'-log-file PATH'
     Append server log output to PATH ('FLOW_API_LOG_FILE').
'-service-name NAME'
     Windows SCM service name when running as a Windows Service
     (default 'GoFlowAPI').
'-secure-key KEY'
     Default AES-256-GCM passphrase ('FLOW_SECURE_KEY').
'-key-file PATH'
     File containing the default AES-256-GCM passphrase.
'-bootstrap-user USER'
     Seed or update an initial BasicAuth user at startup
     ('FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_USER').
'-bootstrap-pass PASS'
     Password for '-bootstrap-user', automatically bcrypt-hashed
     ('FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PASS').
'-bootstrap-perm ROLE'
     Permission role for '-bootstrap-user': 'all' (default),
     'execution-only', 'read-only', 'write', or 'upload'.
'-hash-password PASS'
     Print a bcrypt hash of PASS to stdout and exit.
'-debug'
     Enable verbose debug logging ('FLOW_API_DEBUG').


