4 Configuring OS Services and 'rc' Scripts
******************************************

4.1 Linux ('systemd')
=====================

Linux '.deb', '.rpm', and Arch '.pkg.tar.zst' packages create the
unprivileged 'flowapi' user, install '/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env'
(mode '0640'), and register '/usr/lib/systemd/system/go-flow-api.service':

     sudo vi /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
     sudo systemctl enable --now go-flow-api.service
     sudo systemctl status go-flow-api.service
     sudo journalctl -u go-flow-api.service -f

4.2 Linux (OpenRC and SysVinit)
===============================

For Alpine, Gentoo, Devuan, or SysVinit hosts, ready-to-install init
scripts are bundled under '/opt/flow-api/share/services/openrc/go-flow-api'
and '/opt/flow-api/share/services/sysvinit/go-flow-api'.  Copy the
script to '/etc/init.d/go-flow-api' ('chmod 0755') and enable via
'rc-update add go-flow-api default' (OpenRC) or 'update-rc.d go-flow-api
defaults' / 'chkconfig --add go-flow-api' (SysVinit).

4.3 FreeBSD ('rc.d')
====================

The FreeBSD '.pkg' installs '/usr/local/etc/rc.d/go_flow_api' and seeds
'/usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env':

     sudo vi /usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
     sudo sysrc go_flow_api_enable="YES"
     sudo service go_flow_api start
     sudo service go_flow_api status

4.4 macOS ('launchd')
=====================

Configure '/opt/flow-api/etc/go-flow-api.env' ('chmod 0600'), copy
'/opt/flow-api/share/services/launchd/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist'
into '/Library/LaunchDaemons/', and run:

     sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist
     sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api

4.5 Windows (Native SCM Windows Service)
========================================

'go-flowAPI.exe' natively supports the Windows Service Control Manager.
Run the bundled PowerShell installer in an elevated Administrator shell:

     & "C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow API\share\services\windows\Install-GoFlowAPIService.ps1" -Start


